Bad Database Design Example

| order_id | customer_name | customer_phone | product | product_price | city |
|---:|---|---|---|---:|---|
| 1001 | Arun | 98765 | Laptop | 60000 | Chennai |
| 1002 | Arun | 98765 | Mouse | 1000 | Chennai |
| 1003 | Priya | 91234 | Laptop | 60000 | Bangalore |

What happens if Arun changes his phone number?
We need to update multiple rows.
That creates a risk of inconsistent data.
