4. What is Normalization?
Simple definition:
Normalization is the process of organizing data into related tables to reduce unnecessary duplication and improve data consistency.
Don't store the same fact repeatedly when you can store it once and reference it.

-------------------------------------------------------------
|Why do we need normalization?|

Normalization helps prevent three major problems.

1. Update anomaly
2. Insert anomaly
3.Delete anomaly
