Composite Primary Key

A table can have a primary key made from multiple columns.

CREATE TABLE student_courses (
    student_id INTEGER,
    course_id INTEGER,

    PRIMARY KEY (student_id, course_id)
);

This means:
student_id + course_id
together must be unique.

So:
1 | 101   ✅
1 | 102   ✅
2 | 101   ✅


